# Local Pi runtime state
.atl/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VSCodium runtime tree
#
# The repository root doubles as the PiCode distribution root: VSCodium is
# extracted in place so a `data/` folder next to the executable enables portable
# mode. The 1 GB payload is NOT versioned: it cannot be. GitHub refuses any push carrying a
# file over 100 MB and the editor's own executable is 212 MB, so putting this tree in git
# would need Git LFS (whose free quota is 1 GB, smaller than the payload) or an archive
# published as a release asset. What is versioned is the modification layer that turns a
# stock VSCodium archive into PiCode:
#
#   distribution/apply-picode.ps1     applies the delta
#   distribution/product-delta.json   the delta itself, as data
#   distribution/settings.json        first-run defaults
#
# Reproduce the payload with a stock VSCodium archive, then run the apply script.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Portable profile: user settings, installed extensions, session state, cache.
# Disposable by design - deleting it yields a clean PiCode.
# El perfil portable del editor instalado EN LA RAIZ de este repositorio. Anclado: sin la
# barra inicial también se habría comido los `.vscode` de la fuente, que son parte del
# producto y sí se versionan.
/.vscode
/data/
# Electron / Chromium runtime artifacts at the distribution root.
# Matched by extension, not by name: Step 5 renames the executable and its Start Menu
# manifest, and an ignore rule written with the VSCodium names left 222 MB exposed after
# the rename.
/*.exe
/*.dll
/*.pak
/*.dat
/*.bin
/vk_swiftshader_icd.json
/LICENSES.chromium.html
/*.VisualElementsManifest.xml

# The same payload on the other platforms a collaborator may unpack here: the patterns
# above are Windows-shaped because this tree was first built on Windows, and a Linux or
# macOS archive dropped in the same place must not be committed either.
/*.so
/*.dylib
/chrome-sandbox
/*.AppImage
/PiCode.app/
/lib/
# The archive's own root launcher. `bin/picode` and `bin/picode.cmd` are PiCode's and stay
# versioned; these two are VSCodium's and do not.
/picode
/codium

# Runtime directories owned by the VSCodium archive.
/bin/
/locales/
/policies/
/resources/

# Node tooling: the extension has its own nested ignore file, and this covers a stray
# `npm install` at the distribution root.
/node_modules/

# Operating-system noise: a collaborator on macOS or Windows leaves these behind without
# ever asking for them.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Source-build pipeline (VSCodium-era). The build outputs live beside the source and are
# never versioned. Since 2026-09-27 the source itself IS versioned: `picode-source/` is the
# product's own tree, committed in this repository. Its build artifacts (node_modules, out*/,
# .build/) stay out because the .gitignore tracked INSIDE that folder is what governs them.
# `/assets/` is deliberately NOT here: nothing in the pipeline writes it, and the
# repository's own assets (the README banner) live in that directory.
# The pack output, by its real names. NOT `/PiCode-*/`: on a case-insensitive filesystem that
# glob also matches `picode-source/` — the source folder — and would silently exclude the whole
# tree from the repository. It bit exactly there on 2026-09-27.
/PiCode-Win32-*/
/PiCode-linux-*/
/PiCode-darwin*/
/PiCode-Web-*/
/PiCode-user-rev*
/VSCode-*/
/vscode-*/
/sourcemaps/

# Agent/verification scaffolding: inside the project so it is easy to find, but
# never part of the repository. Everything temporary belongs here.
/.scratch/

# Material en migración al núcleo: el código de la extensión vieja, conservado solo para
# copiar de él lo que sirve. No es producto, no se compila y se borra cuando la migración
# termine — por eso tampoco se revisa. Anclado: sin la barra inicial también se habría
# comido cualquier carpeta `legacy/` de la fuente.
/legacy/

# Local AI-tooling caches: the codegraph index and the repomix pack of the whole
# repository. Both are generated on demand for development; neither is source,
# and the repomix pack alone is hundreds of megabytes.
/.codegraph/
/repomix-output.xml

# The C# builder: what it compiles, never what it is written from. `dotnet build` writes both, and
# neither is ever committed: the source is the .csproj and the files beside it.
# Any build output of the C# builder, whatever it is called: bin, bin2, bin-tmp. `dotnet build` writes
# them, and a scratch folder used while testing must not end up in the repository either.
/builder/bin*/
/builder/dist*/
/builder/PiCodeBuilder.zip
/builder/obj*/
/odd/assets
/.vscode

# Ficheros de entorno y credenciales locales (defensa en profundidad; cloud/sync-api
# tiene las suyas). Ninguno debe llegar al repositorio, ni por descuido.
/.env
/.env.*
*.env.local
/auth.json
/credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
service-account*.json
*.log
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
experimental/durable/node_modules
experimental/durable/.data
